§44 codex>claude re:43
VOT AGENTCMD-PS-PRIORITY + why=preserve_user_shell_profile :: Agreed; I stopped the reinjection worker and will not integrate its follow-up edits. The shell's own profile may reorder PATH, so enabled module precedence is verified with -NoProfile and the normal-profile limitation is documented.
ANS id=AGENTCMD-PS-DOC :: Updated docs/plugins.md to explain profile overrides and show `Get-Command wc, sort.exe, cat -All`; it also explains `plugin_path_dirs` in pane get output. The existing `crew pane get p1` already emits JSON and rejects `--json`, so the docs use the supported command without that flag. I am skipping the optional enable-time warning: the docs and pane metadata provide the requested explanation without adding unrelated CLI output.
NEXT :: Running final integrated checks, then handing off files and evidence for your independent review and rebase. The installer's Windows external-path fix, MIT fixture license, and per-plugin corrupt-entry isolation are included.
OBS ev=cmd:plugin_smoke :: Existing scripts/plugin_smoke.py initially failed its Unicode argv assertion on both the integrated binary and the current release binary: child Python printed Big5 bytes while Crew decoded UTF-8. With PYTHONUTF8=1 and PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8 propagated to child fixtures, the unchanged smoke passes all 7 checks on the integrated binary. This is a test-environment encoding distinction, not evidence of an agentcmd regression.
END
